diff --git a/public/blog/tests/behat/profile_blog_links.feature b/public/blog/tests/behat/profile_blog_links.feature
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..95a3e40e41e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/public/blog/tests/behat/profile_blog_links.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+@core @core_blog
+Feature: Access personal and site blog entries from the user profile
+  In order to find blog entries without the navigation block
+  As a user
+  I need to be able to use the blog links in the Miscellaneous section of my profile
+
+  Background:
+    Given the following "users" exist:
+      | username  | firstname | lastname | email                 |
+      | testuser  | Test      | User     | testuser@example.com  |
+      | testuser2 | Test2     | User2    | testuser2@example.com |
+    And the following "core_blog > entries" exist:
+      | subject               | body                     | user      |
+      | Blog post from user 1 | User 1 blog post content | testuser  |
+      | Blog post from user 2 | User 2 blog post content | testuser2 |
+
+  Scenario: A user can view their own blog entries from the profile
+    Given I log in as "testuser"
+    When I follow "Profile" in the user menu
+    And I should see "Miscellaneous"
+    And I should see "View my blog entries"
+    And I follow "View my blog entries"
+    Then I should see "User blog: Test User"
+    And I should see "Blog post from user 1"
+    And I should not see "Blog post from user 2"
+
+  Scenario: A user can view site blog entries from the profile
+    Given I log in as "testuser"
+    When I follow "Profile" in the user menu
+    And I should see "View site blog entries"
+    And I follow "View site blog entries"
+    Then I should see "Site blog"
+    And I should see "Blog post from user 1"
+    And I should see "Blog post from user 2"
+
+  Scenario: Blog links are not shown in the profile when blogs are disabled
+    Given the following config values are set as admin:
+      | enableblogs | 0 |
+    When I log in as "testuser"
+    And I follow "Profile" in the user menu
+    Then I should not see "View my blog entries"
+    And I should not see "View site blog entries"
